  "tagline": "In-memory relational database that runs your server logic as WASM modules and streams changes to clients.",
  "description": "SpacetimeDB, from Clockwork Labs, combines a relational database and an application server: you write modules in Rust, C# or TypeScript whose reducers run inside the database as transactions, and clients subscribe to SQL queries and receive live updates over WebSockets. Data is held in memory with a commit log and snapshots for durability, which gives very low latency for state-heavy apps. It was built to run the MMO BitCraft and is now marketed as a reactive backend platform with a managed Maincloud. The BSL licence restricts offering it as a competing hosted service.",
